I also see the same error as [hebasto](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35855#issuecomment-5184565563) and Jan on aarch64.

@janb84 fix seems interesting (in that it works), but it was a different direction than I was looking. ISTM that a compiler with a static libc should have no includes to fix, so not running `fixincludes` should be the goal (of a fix).  Maybe something more like https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/be6c6c5a006c0b8ba3107f78926eef570726b15f

Even more ideal could be for this to be upstreamed into `cross-gcc` which could automatically add --disable-fixincludes whenever libc is false or something.
